{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/750677-jovian-athanors","id":750677,"title":"Jovian Athanors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-02T21:45:37-08:00","id":750677,"title":"Jovian Athanors","content":"Honestly, these &quot;Athanors of Flux&quot; seem the most interesting part of the new preview. Instant plot hook factory!<br /> <br /> Still, I can't help but wonder a couple things:<br /> <br /> 1) How are they made? The phrase &quot;seeks to shed the negative emotions&quot; make it sound like they're a product of a Dramatic Failure on a Torment roll (not only does the Promethean not deal with the rising destabilization, s/he actually rejects part of it entirely, and it becomes grounded somewhere nearby). But it also sounds like something that could happen when embracing Stannum, particularly if that is part of refusing Flux (Centimani always struck me as being an immensely self-loathing path in 2E; realizing you aren't to blame for what's happened to you means that self-directed aggression and anxiety has to go <i>somewhere</i>).<br /> <br /> 2) Can they be made deliberately? I can see a particularly barmy alchemist or Centimanus cooking one up just to see if they could-and then to control its effects as a weapon. I have this lovely idea of one Freak who imbued one with her disgust for humanity's tendency towards unfettered destruction in pursuit of their goals; everywhere it influences, humans and those closely related become subject to distinctly vampiric frenzies in which they become preternaturally able and utterly amoral when faced with something they desperately want, should they give into the urge-which the Centimanus can trigger increasingly easily the more they give into the Athanor, to pursue <i>her </i>desires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T13:43:49-08:00","id":752175,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'll get in trouble for saying that I include a Jovian Athanor in my Dark Ages Companion work as a plot device. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T17:10:06-08:00","id":752476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/750677-jovian-athanors?p=752175#post752175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I'll get in trouble for saying that I include a Jovian Athanor in my Dark Ages Companion work as a plot device. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... now we just need to know which one you are working :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:20:16-08:00","id":752875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/750677-jovian-athanors#post750677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, these &quot;Athanors of Flux&quot; seem the most interesting part of the new preview. Instant plot hook factory!<br /> <br /> Still, I can't help but wonder a couple things:<br /> <br /> 1) How are they made? The phrase &quot;seeks to shed the negative emotions&quot; make it sound like they're a product of a Dramatic Failure on a Torment roll (not only does the Promethean not deal with the rising destabilization, s/he actually rejects part of it entirely, and it becomes grounded somewhere nearby). But it also sounds like something that could happen when embracing Stannum, particularly if that is part of refusing Flux (Centimani always struck me as being an immensely self-loathing path in 2E; realizing you aren't to blame for what's happened to you means that self-directed aggression and anxiety has to go <i>somewhere</i>).<br /> <br /> 2) Can they be made deliberately? I can see a particularly barmy alchemist or Centimanus cooking one up just to see if they could-and then to control its effects as a weapon. I have this lovely idea of one Freak who imbued one with her disgust for humanity's tendency towards unfettered destruction in pursuit of their goals; everywhere it influences, humans and those closely related become subject to distinctly vampiric frenzies in which they become preternaturally able and utterly amoral when faced with something they desperately want, should they give into the urge-which the Centimanus can trigger increasingly easily the more they give into the Athanor, to pursue <i>her </i>desires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> #1 definitely seems plausible. And seeing as the GMC systems allow you to turn failures into dramatic failures, perhaps it could be deliberate in part. As for making it intentionally, I wouldn't remove that possibility, though it would definitely be a breaking point for non-Centimani and any mortal alchemist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:47:03-08:00","id":754621,"title":"","content":"It's not like Promethean to allow you to shed baggage at will, which would make both options seem...optimistic? Like, for #1, not so much a Dramatic Failure, but instead a failed Milestone or a loss of Pilgrimage (assuming it's close enough to olde Humanity to have such a mechanic). Remember, you can drop a fail to a botch for a Beat, and if you can spit your Torment out into a disposable thing while escaping the burdens that caused it, why wouldn't you?<br /> <br /> #2 seems like a possibility, though, but only for Centimani, and even then, they'd be shedding a personal cause of bitterness and despair, and there's only so many times you can do that before the entire endeavor loses its shine. Meanwhile, Furies seem like they'd pop Jovians like they were candy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T05:29:17-08:00","id":758459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/750677-jovian-athanors?p=752476#post752476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... now we just need to know which one you are working :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Thirty Years War. ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:29:20-08:00","id":758633,"title":"","content":"Ooh, well that's a bad sign. The hints of what Jovian Athanors do is enough reason to not be particularly thrilled about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T08:23:23-08:00","id":758679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/750677-jovian-athanors?p=758633#post758633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, well that's a bad sign. The hints of what Jovian Athanors do is enough reason to not be particularly thrilled about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I second that. It makes you wonder what <i>other</i> conflicts got kicked off because of a Jovian Athanor conveniently present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:28:46-08:00","id":774366,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else remember the bad candy story seed from Urban legends? <br /> <br /> A woman, I guess a witch or folk magic user or something, is able to extract traumatic memories and store them physically, currently she's using candy. <br /> <br /> She's not, however, above selling this candy to people who want the trauma. <br /> <br /> Perhaps in a promethean game she could be a well meaning alchemist who doesn't understand why making jovian athanors is a bad idea, or perhaps she has a method to dilute flux athanors so they are safer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}